}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $(P∧¬Q)⇒(P∨¬Q).$ This statement is true unless $P∧¬Q$ is true and $P∨¬Q$ is false.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P∧¬Q\\,$ | $\\,P∨¬Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∧¬Q)⇒(P∨¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572151 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572151 #edb/ref 1069 "q-103483" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572151 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572151 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. **If** $3+5=7,$ **then** $2+4=7.$\n\nII. **If** $3+4=7,$ **then** $3+2=6.$\n\nIII. **If** $3+2=4,$ **then** $2+5=7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572151 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d3a8865-856a-528d-95c1-4dd040a3ff92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572151 #edb/ref 1074 "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true. The antecedent $3+5=7$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. The antecedent $3+4=7$ is true, and the consequent $3+2=6$ is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Again, the antecedent $3+2=4$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572190 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182670" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572190 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572190 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∨¬B)⇒A\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572190 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1bfba5d-aabc-58c5-979a-9057330a8d86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572190 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we add columns for $¬B$ and $A∨¬B:$\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ | $\\,A∨¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $(A∨¬B)⇒A.$ This statement is true unless $A∨¬B$ is true and $A$ is false.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬B\\,$ | $\\,A∨¬B\\,$ | $\\,(A∨¬B)⇒A\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
